Start a data channel over when a packet comes from far behind.

The packet window ignores a packet behind its newest one as already played, and the audio
channel drops a frame behind the one it expects next. If either position gets ahead of the
stream, every later packet is dropped too, until the 16-bit ids wrap: the sound goes silent for
minutes while the video plays on.

A packet further behind than the window holds, or an audio frame more than 256 behind (about
2.5 s), now makes the channel start over from it, as one too far ahead already does (0020). The
control channel still ignores late packets, since a resend that late is a copy.

